WEBVTT

00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:35.958
<i>Shakin', sugar, sugar!</i>

00:00:35.958 --> 00:00:37.917
<i>Shakin', sugar, sugar!</i>

00:00:41.333 --> 00:00:42.917
<i>Shakin', sugar, sugar!</i>

00:00:42.917 --> 00:00:44.750
<i>Shakin', sugar, sugar!</i>

00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:48.417
<i>Shake it love, YES!</i>

00:00:48.417 --> 00:00:51.958
<i>I'm going crazy with longing</i>

00:00:51.958 --> 00:00:53.542
<i>Brushing back my hair</i>

00:00:53.542 --> 00:00:55.583
<i>That got wet in an instant</i>

00:00:55.583 --> 00:00:58.250
<i>Being toyed with by the warm rain</i>

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:01.750
<i>Shall I see how far I can run?</i>

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:03.708
<i>The prayer</i>

00:01:03.708 --> 00:01:05.708
<i>That spun out</i>

00:01:05.708 --> 00:01:08.625
<i>Connects to the future</i>

00:01:08.625 --> 00:01:09.542
<i>Overflowing</i>

00:01:09.542 --> 00:01:11.083
<i>The miracle of love</i>

00:01:11.083 --> 00:01:13.000
<i>The wonderful miracle</i>

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.792
<i>The voice of these six flowers</i>

00:01:15.792 --> 00:01:18.000
<i>is released! (Shake it love, SAY!)</i>

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.833
<i>Pulling toward each other (So fast!)</i>

00:01:19.833 --> 00:01:21.500
<i>That power (So vast!)</i>

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:23.792
<i>I want it to reach you</i>

00:01:23.792 --> 00:01:25.083
<i>Don't stop the music</i>

00:01:25.083 --> 00:01:26.917
<i>High in the night sky (So high!)</i>

00:01:26.917 --> 00:01:29.000
<i>I send up my excitement (Turn round!)</i>

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.458
<i>Gravitic-romantic</i>

00:01:31.458 --> 00:01:32.250
<i>Tonight</i>

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.917
<i>Can't be stopped (Nonstop!)</i>

00:01:33.917 --> 00:01:35.708
<i>The impulse of love (Get down!)</i>

00:01:35.708 --> 00:01:38.833
<i>I want to mess you up</i>

00:01:38.833 --> 00:01:40.542
<i>T-T-Take it easy now!</i>

00:01:40.542 --> 00:01:42.167
<i>To embrace you</i>

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:43.833
<i>a-a-as I feel it</i>

00:01:43.833 --> 00:01:44.583
<i>Let's dance</i>

00:01:44.583 --> 00:01:47.833
<i>And once you're captivated, kiss!</i>

00:01:47.833 --> 00:01:49.583
<i>Good love! Good love!</i>

00:01:49.583 --> 00:01:52.000
<i>Gravitic-love!</i>

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.792
<i>Shakin', sugar, sugar!</i>

00:01:53.792 --> 00:01:55.708
<i>Shakin', sugar, sugar!</i>

00:01:56.875 --> 00:01:59.167
<i>Shake it love, YES!</i>

00:02:02.458 --> 00:02:04.333
"The Hajime Mutsuki Expedition"

00:02:04.333 --> 00:02:06.875
"The Hajime Mutsuki Expedition"
Wasn't that bridge the only way

00:02:06.875 --> 00:02:08.792
"The Hajime Mutsuki Expedition"
to get to and from the island?

00:02:08.792 --> 00:02:10.833
And that burned up.

00:02:10.833 --> 00:02:12.750
Which means--

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:15.000
We're stuck here...

00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:24.750
Yes, that's right, everyone's fine.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:27.500
No one's hurt.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:28.500
Yes.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.875
For now, in order to get off the island...

00:02:33.958 --> 00:02:35.375
Hello?

00:02:37.375 --> 00:02:39.875
"Call ended"
"Mr. Tsukishiro"

00:03:00.083 --> 00:03:02.708
We cannot leave the island,

00:03:02.708 --> 00:03:05.292
nor can we contact anyone off the island.

00:03:05.292 --> 00:03:07.792
What should we do in this situation?

00:03:07.792 --> 00:03:10.042
We should secure our lifelines, right?

00:03:10.042 --> 00:03:11.083
Yes.

00:03:11.083 --> 00:03:14.083
We have no electricity,
and our phones don't work, either.

00:03:14.083 --> 00:03:16.583
Our gas is propane, so that's fine.

00:03:16.583 --> 00:03:18.000
As for water...

00:03:19.917 --> 00:03:21.458
No problem.

00:03:22.542 --> 00:03:28.792
There was a tank on top of the cottage,
so we should be fine until that's gone.

00:03:28.792 --> 00:03:31.167
Yeah, it should last at least a day.

00:03:31.167 --> 00:03:32.750
What about food?

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:35.375
We made curry for dinner.

00:03:35.375 --> 00:03:37.375
Why don't we eat?

00:03:39.125 --> 00:03:41.208
"*To all good boys and girls: You must not
feed curry to rabbits. -Hajime Mutsuki"

00:03:43.042 --> 00:03:45.625
You again?!

00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:47.292
--Oh dear.
--Come back here, Kuroda!

00:03:47.292 --> 00:03:51.417
Aw, I was looking forward
to the Midsummer Gena Curry!

00:03:51.417 --> 00:03:55.125
And actually, I was pretty proud of today's.

00:03:55.125 --> 00:03:59.125
Kuroda... You have an infinite stomach.

00:04:01.542 --> 00:04:04.792
If we collect all the snacks and
food souvenirs everyone has,

00:04:04.792 --> 00:04:07.500
we should be okay for at least tonight.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:10.375
But, if it comes down to it...

00:04:11.583 --> 00:04:14.167
Haru. Stop that.

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:17.042
Oh, I was just joking.

00:04:17.042 --> 00:04:19.792
Now, what shall we do?

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:25.042
Since it's just for the night, I think
it would be best to sit tight here.

00:04:25.042 --> 00:04:28.083
Oh, it looks like the rain's stopped.

00:04:28.083 --> 00:04:30.292
It's still pretty windy, though.

00:04:36.125 --> 00:04:37.542
Over there!

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:43.750
This is bad. We'll lose all the water.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.625
Let's stop it up with something!

00:04:45.625 --> 00:04:50.125
We've fixed it temporarily,
but the water is still leaking.

00:04:50.125 --> 00:04:52.125
I don't know how long it'll last...

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:54.833
This is a serious turn of events.

00:04:54.833 --> 00:04:56.250
What should we do?

00:04:57.792 --> 00:05:01.208
Let's find some containers
and put the water in them.

00:05:01.208 --> 00:05:07.167
Once that's done, we can see if there are any
tools in this house we can use to fix the tank.

00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:08.208
Yeah.

00:05:08.208 --> 00:05:09.625
Got it!

00:05:10.667 --> 00:05:13.792
Let's wash these pots so we can
use them for the water.

00:05:13.792 --> 00:05:15.000
Roger.

00:05:28.958 --> 00:05:31.542
What's wrong, little ones?

00:05:31.542 --> 00:05:35.417
Th-Th-There was a strange sound outside!

00:05:35.417 --> 00:05:38.000
A strange sound?

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:42.458
It sounded like branches breaking
and something coming close...

00:05:42.458 --> 00:05:44.875
Couldn't that have been the wind?

00:05:47.958 --> 00:05:49.792
See, it's the wind.

00:05:49.792 --> 00:05:53.167
Was that all? They like to make
a big deal out of nothing.

00:05:53.167 --> 00:05:56.167
B-But there really <i>was </i>a weird sound!

00:05:56.167 --> 00:05:57.833
Wasn't that just the wind, too--

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:08.000
I definitely heard something that
sounded like the cry of an animal...

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:10.042
And the sound of branches breaking!

00:06:10.042 --> 00:06:13.458
Like a giant creature was going through
the forest and stepping on trees!

00:06:13.458 --> 00:06:15.417
Ikkun, stop it!

00:06:15.417 --> 00:06:17.917
It's true that that's what it sounded like.

00:06:17.917 --> 00:06:21.917
A sound hard to go near.
The sound of something huge.

00:06:21.917 --> 00:06:25.375
From the living room,
we couldn't hear anything, right?

00:06:25.375 --> 00:06:28.750
Lightning, a blackout, and a broken tank.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:30.500
And now maybe even a monster?

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:32.292
Things have gotten interesting!

00:06:32.292 --> 00:06:35.167
Shun, stop thinking this is fun.

00:06:35.167 --> 00:06:37.417
I feel like it'll make unnecessary things happen.

00:06:37.417 --> 00:06:41.708
The cause of that roar
can't also be Kuroda, can it?

00:06:41.708 --> 00:06:44.583
Huh? Does Kuroda make sounds?

00:06:44.583 --> 00:06:46.208
I've never heard any...

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:49.500
Speaking of which, where <i>is </i>Kuroda?

00:06:52.667 --> 00:06:53.875
Kuroda!

00:06:53.875 --> 00:06:55.125
Kuroda...

00:06:55.125 --> 00:06:56.375
--Where are you?
--Kuroda!

00:06:56.375 --> 00:06:57.375
Kuroda!

00:06:58.917 --> 00:07:00.542
Nowhere to be found, huh?

00:07:00.542 --> 00:07:02.250
Don't tell me he was eaten by that monster...

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:03.667
Stop that!

00:07:04.375 --> 00:07:07.042
--Kuroda!
--Kuroda!

00:07:07.042 --> 00:07:07.875
Kuroda!

00:07:07.875 --> 00:07:08.667
Kuro!

00:07:08.667 --> 00:07:10.208
Kuroda!

00:07:12.292 --> 00:07:16.250
For now, we have the water we need to survive.

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:20.875
Help should come in the morning,
so we should be able to get by somehow.

00:07:20.875 --> 00:07:23.625
I'm glad I bought snacks for souvenirs.

00:07:23.625 --> 00:07:27.083
Once we can get off the island,
let's go buy them again.

00:07:29.958 --> 00:07:32.042
I'm going out for a bit.

00:07:32.042 --> 00:07:33.917
Are you going to look for Kuroda?

00:07:33.917 --> 00:07:37.375
Yes. He caused some trouble,

00:07:37.375 --> 00:07:40.208
but I am partly responsible
for bringing him without noticing.

00:07:40.208 --> 00:07:41.792
Then, let's look for him together.

00:07:41.792 --> 00:07:44.042
No, it's fine.

00:07:44.042 --> 00:07:46.208
I'll just go by myself for now.

00:07:46.208 --> 00:07:48.333
Wait a minute, Hajime.

00:07:51.042 --> 00:07:53.083
Look at this.

00:07:53.083 --> 00:07:55.833
This is the cottage where we are right now.

00:07:55.833 --> 00:07:59.000
This is the bridge. Now look at this--

00:07:59.917 --> 00:08:03.417
It looks like this island has a pier.

00:08:03.417 --> 00:08:06.292
Kuroda could be there, huh?

00:08:06.292 --> 00:08:07.625
That's true.

00:08:07.625 --> 00:08:12.583
Oh, a pier might have tools
for fixing boats, too, right?

00:08:13.792 --> 00:08:20.458
Yeah, so how about looking for Kuroda
while we look for the tools?

00:08:26.792 --> 00:08:30.625
Fine. Let's split up and go to the pier.

00:08:30.625 --> 00:08:32.875
But we'll do it in teams.

00:08:32.875 --> 00:08:33.958
Of course!

00:08:33.958 --> 00:08:36.333
Yeah, that sounds good.

00:08:36.333 --> 00:08:39.458
I'll take the route going
through the forest to the pier.

00:08:39.458 --> 00:08:43.667
It's a little further, but a group
should follow the shoreline of the island.

00:08:43.667 --> 00:08:48.000
Leave that to me.
How do you want to choose teams?

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.542
Let's see.

00:08:49.542 --> 00:08:53.000
Kai, I want you to prioritize
fixing the hole on the roof's tank.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:57.667
Roger. I'll keep trying to fix it
with the tools we have here.

00:08:57.667 --> 00:09:00.750
We'll split everyone else up
fairly by drawing lots.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:03.583
What?! I'm on the same team as Kakeru?

00:09:03.583 --> 00:09:04.042
"Mountain Crossing Team"

00:09:04.042 --> 00:09:06.208
"Mountain Crossing Team"
Oh, are you unhappy about that, Ikkun?

00:09:06.208 --> 00:09:08.917
"Mountain Crossing Team"
Oh no, but...

00:09:08.917 --> 00:09:12.958
"Mountain Crossing Team"
Please, don't activate your bad luck this time...

00:09:12.958 --> 00:09:14.042
"Mountain Crossing Team"
Just kidding...

00:09:14.042 --> 00:09:15.250
"Mountain Crossing Team"
Don't worry!

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:18.833
As long as we have Hajime,
he'll negate my unlucky-ness!

00:09:18.833 --> 00:09:19.917
Probably!

00:09:19.917 --> 00:09:23.542
You really are optimistic.

00:09:23.542 --> 00:09:26.333
I suppose we are the cautious team.

00:09:26.333 --> 00:09:27.208
"Coast Crossing Team"

00:09:27.208 --> 00:09:30.167
"Coast Crossing Team"
Let's decide on the time limit in advance.

00:09:30.167 --> 00:09:33.375
If the other team doesn't
get to the pier in that time,

00:09:33.375 --> 00:09:38.833
then the other team will come back
to the cottage using the other route.

00:09:38.833 --> 00:09:44.167
That way, if something happens to one team,
the other team can save them.

00:09:44.167 --> 00:09:46.875
Good idea, Haru!

00:09:46.875 --> 00:09:49.542
The remaining members should help Kai.

00:09:49.542 --> 00:09:50.708
Okay.

00:09:50.708 --> 00:09:52.917
Well then, let's go.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:58.708
"Emergency operation! Gravi & Procella"

00:09:58.708 --> 00:10:01.500
"Emergency operation! Gravi & Procella"
"Emergency operation! Gravi and Procella!"

00:10:02.792 --> 00:10:07.167
"Encounter in a dense forest: Expose the
true form of the mysterious giant creature!"

00:10:08.167 --> 00:10:09.500
Based on the testimony of the local boys,

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:14.875
we, the film crew, set out on
a search for the giant creature.

00:10:14.875 --> 00:10:18.667
However, unimaginable difficulties awaited us!

00:10:18.667 --> 00:10:20.500
Hey, what's that?!

00:10:23.042 --> 00:10:25.292
"The giant creature standing in
the way of Gravi & Procella!"

00:10:28.458 --> 00:10:29.917
"The mysterious voice that resounds
through the forest of the solitary isle"

00:10:30.333 --> 00:10:31.458
Ouch!

00:10:31.458 --> 00:10:33.667
"Will the boys be able to survive?!!"

00:10:37.042 --> 00:10:37.208
"We were washing pots in the kitchen"

00:10:37.208 --> 00:10:41.083
"We were washing pots in the kitchen"
My name is Ren. Once upon a time.

00:10:41.083 --> 00:10:45.042
"when we heard the cry of an animal."
This is a pen. How much, please?

00:10:45.042 --> 00:10:48.667
"Then there was the sound of breaking branches,"
I'm, don't, not, ear reading, crack, crack.

00:10:48.667 --> 00:10:50.833
"and it felt like something was coming closer..."
I'm, don't, not, ear reading, crack, crack.

00:10:51.042 --> 00:10:54.042
"That wasn't a cow or a dog."
Okay. Turn left

00:10:54.042 --> 00:10:57.208
"I think it was something bigger."
and go straight, please.

00:10:59.708 --> 00:11:05.875
We, the film crew, went toward the forest
where the giant creature's roar was heard.

00:11:05.875 --> 00:11:10.125
"Does the giant creature really exist?"

00:11:10.125 --> 00:11:12.250
thought Captain Hajime.

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:16.000
He could not allow anyone
to be injured on this expedition.

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:18.583
Not a single light lit the path they were on.

00:11:18.583 --> 00:11:22.583
One step at a time, they advanced carefully.

00:11:22.583 --> 00:11:26.750
And then suddenly, a strange scene
unfolded before our eyes!

00:11:30.167 --> 00:11:31.792
There are broken branches.

00:11:31.792 --> 00:11:34.458
This must have been what you heard.

00:11:34.458 --> 00:11:37.083
This looks freshly broken.

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:42.542
Wait, Hajime! Please be careful!

00:11:42.542 --> 00:11:43.833
It's dangerous!

00:11:43.833 --> 00:11:48.125
Even if it were, we cannot just
stand around at the entrance of the forest.

00:11:48.125 --> 00:11:50.000
That's true, but...

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:54.625
We, the film crew, advanced
even more carefully into the forest.

00:11:55.750 --> 00:12:01.708
The path was rugged, as if nature itself
was trying to block our intrusion.

00:12:01.708 --> 00:12:05.250
Shut off from the light of the moon
in the completely dark forest,

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:08.417
human intellect could not help us.

00:12:08.417 --> 00:12:14.250
The muddy path with extreme height changes
stole our strength mercilessly.

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:15.750
We were at our limit.

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:18.292
It would be better if we turned back.

00:12:18.292 --> 00:12:19.833
Just as we all thought this--

00:12:21.750 --> 00:12:23.167
What's wrong?!

00:12:25.333 --> 00:12:26.958
Kakeru's gone!

00:12:32.542 --> 00:12:37.125
Suddenly, a giant cave
appeared before our eyes.

00:12:37.125 --> 00:12:40.708
Could this be where the giant creature dwelled?

00:12:40.708 --> 00:12:43.708
And was the vanished Kakeru all right?

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:51.667
Is this where Kakeru fell?

00:12:51.667 --> 00:12:52.875
Yes.

00:12:52.875 --> 00:12:57.667
You almost have to respect
how unlucky Kakeru is.

00:12:57.667 --> 00:13:01.542
Hey! You alive?

00:13:01.542 --> 00:13:03.333
I'm alive!

00:13:03.333 --> 00:13:07.667
There were piles of dried grass
and stuff, so I'm not hurt!

00:13:08.667 --> 00:13:11.083
It looks like the tunnel that was on the map.

00:13:11.667 --> 00:13:12.083
"Impassable - Risk of Collapse"

00:13:12.083 --> 00:13:13.625
"Impassable - Risk of Collapse"
Look, over there.

00:13:13.625 --> 00:13:16.083
"Impassable - Risk of Collapse"
A rotten floor?

00:13:16.083 --> 00:13:18.250
There's a ladder here.

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:28.042
I'm saved!

00:13:28.042 --> 00:13:32.708
I wish you wouldn't activate your
unlucky mode at a time like this, though.

00:13:32.708 --> 00:13:35.833
It's not like I <i>wanted </i>to choose this fate!

00:13:35.833 --> 00:13:37.167
I know, I know.

00:13:37.167 --> 00:13:39.333
Go on, climb up first.

00:13:49.958 --> 00:13:51.292
Kakeru...

00:13:52.542 --> 00:13:54.625
You sure are lucky, Kakeru...

00:13:56.417 --> 00:13:59.250
Well, Hajime, what should we do?

00:14:01.375 --> 00:14:04.083
Go into <i>that</i>...?

00:14:04.083 --> 00:14:05.417
What?!

00:14:05.417 --> 00:14:08.708
If the tunnel collapses,
there's nowhere else we can run.

00:14:10.042 --> 00:14:14.667
Since there was a floor up above,
I don't think this place will cave in.

00:14:14.667 --> 00:14:18.208
If we go further in,
there might be a path to the surface.

00:14:18.208 --> 00:14:19.417
Look.

00:14:20.958 --> 00:14:23.083
There's wind blowing from the back.

00:14:23.083 --> 00:14:25.042
It's connected to somewhere.

00:14:25.042 --> 00:14:26.542
I see.

00:14:27.917 --> 00:14:29.333
Let's go.

00:14:35.917 --> 00:14:38.292
Let's climb up from here.

00:14:52.083 --> 00:14:53.833
I've checked the footholds.

00:14:53.833 --> 00:14:57.167
If you follow the path I took,
you should be able to climb all the way up.

00:14:57.167 --> 00:14:58.583
Come!

00:15:05.792 --> 00:15:07.292
Okay, next!

00:15:19.542 --> 00:15:21.417
What's this wind?

00:15:23.083 --> 00:15:24.708
This sound is--

00:15:24.708 --> 00:15:27.208
So this was the cry that you guys heard?

00:15:27.208 --> 00:15:29.125
The sound's coming from there!

00:15:32.792 --> 00:15:35.500
It's dangerous to stay here.
Hurry up and come up!

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:36.917
Right!

00:15:46.292 --> 00:15:46.833
You!

00:15:46.833 --> 00:15:47.958
You!

00:15:48.917 --> 00:15:51.042
Another strong gust of wind is coming!

00:15:53.250 --> 00:15:59.292
Idiot. If I give up on you here, my popularity
with the girls will drop like a rock.

00:15:59.292 --> 00:16:01.083
You...

00:16:01.083 --> 00:16:02.583
You can do it!

00:16:02.583 --> 00:16:05.042
A hundredfold!

00:16:29.167 --> 00:16:30.958
That was close...

00:16:30.958 --> 00:16:34.042
Man, I was really nervous for a second there.

00:16:34.042 --> 00:16:36.333
But what was that wind, anyway?

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:46.375
That's...

00:16:46.375 --> 00:16:49.250
...the truth behind
the giant creature's footsteps.

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:51.167
That's what it looks like.

00:16:51.167 --> 00:16:52.583
Look at that.

00:17:05.833 --> 00:17:09.667
It looks like a building made
to generate wind power.

00:17:09.667 --> 00:17:12.167
It appears to be abandoned, though.

00:17:12.167 --> 00:17:16.958
Hmm, it looks like it broke down
and was abandoned like that.

00:17:16.958 --> 00:17:19.667
So the windmills were being
held in place with chains?

00:17:19.667 --> 00:17:21.583
Where the chains broke,

00:17:21.583 --> 00:17:25.375
strong gusts of wind turned the windmills.

00:17:25.375 --> 00:17:28.708
That wind echoed as it passed
through the tunnel,

00:17:28.708 --> 00:17:32.000
making it sound like a monster's roar, huh?

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:34.250
And the sound of trees being knocked down

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:37.375
was caused by the boulders falling
from the collapsing tunnel.

00:17:40.708 --> 00:17:42.083
That's...

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:48.542
You were hiding,

00:17:48.542 --> 00:17:52.125
but then you were so scared of the sound
that you couldn't come back out, huh?

00:17:52.125 --> 00:17:55.750
It's like how the ghost turns out to be
dry grass when you look carefully, huh?

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:57.042
What does that mean?

00:17:57.042 --> 00:18:00.208
It means that once you know the truth
about something, it's not a big deal.

00:18:00.208 --> 00:18:03.458
Come, the pier is up ahead. Hurry!

00:18:12.375 --> 00:18:14.167
You're finally here.

00:18:14.167 --> 00:18:17.208
Oh, Kuroda, too. I'm glad you're okay.

00:18:18.042 --> 00:18:20.167
There are no boats.

00:18:20.167 --> 00:18:21.583
Over there...

00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:26.583
The rope was loosened because of
the heavy rain earlier, huh?

00:18:26.583 --> 00:18:27.750
Yeah...

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:31.458
At this rate, it might get washed far away.

00:18:31.458 --> 00:18:33.583
We can still catch up with it if it's there!

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:36.333
Oof!

00:18:36.333 --> 00:18:37.750
You!

00:18:40.125 --> 00:18:44.750
Whew, this is pretty hard work.
But I'm almost there!

00:18:54.958 --> 00:18:56.375
All right, I made it.

00:19:00.958 --> 00:19:03.000
I caught it!

00:19:08.167 --> 00:19:09.833
Huh? You?

00:19:11.333 --> 00:19:13.167
What the heck was that?!

00:19:13.167 --> 00:19:14.500
Huh?

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:16.083
Look at this!

00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:19.042
That's...

00:19:19.042 --> 00:19:21.000
It's Kai!

00:19:29.583 --> 00:19:34.250
After you all left, I found a new map.

00:19:34.250 --> 00:19:37.958
There was a path that led to the pier
that didn't go through the forest.

00:19:37.958 --> 00:19:39.917
Well? What about those fish?

00:19:39.917 --> 00:19:44.083
I found this spear with all the tools
over there, so I borrowed it.

00:19:44.083 --> 00:19:46.000
It was like I could catch
as many fish as I wanted!

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:50.167
As long as we have this much,
we should be able to feed ten guys, right?

00:19:51.125 --> 00:19:52.083
"Calling"
"Mr. Tsukishiro"

00:19:52.667 --> 00:19:54.750
Yes, this is Mutsuki.

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:56.833
Yes, everyone is fine.

00:19:57.833 --> 00:20:01.500
I understand. Sorry for worrying you.

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:03.125
That was Mr. Tsukishiro.

00:20:03.125 --> 00:20:05.667
He said a boat would reach this island soon.

00:20:05.667 --> 00:20:08.917
Oh, then we need to finish eating these fish!

00:20:08.917 --> 00:20:10.208
Yay!

00:20:10.208 --> 00:20:13.208
We had quite a bit of exercise,
so I'm pretty hungry.

00:20:13.208 --> 00:20:15.917
I was trying to do something cool,

00:20:15.917 --> 00:20:18.625
but it's like Kai stole the show.

00:20:18.625 --> 00:20:20.292
What's that supposed to mean?

00:20:20.292 --> 00:20:22.542
Here, the fish are done. They're delicious!

00:20:27.958 --> 00:20:30.083
Thanks for the food!

00:20:33.583 --> 00:20:35.000
Hey!

00:20:41.625 --> 00:20:46.500
This expedition ended without
anyone getting hurt.

00:20:46.500 --> 00:20:50.208
We could not confirm the
existence of the giant creature,

00:20:50.208 --> 00:20:52.750
but there was no mistake
that the truth created by nature

00:20:52.750 --> 00:20:58.000
had gone beyond what we,
the film crew, had imagined.

00:20:58.000 --> 00:20:59.875
Like the one on this on journey,

00:20:59.875 --> 00:21:06.458
a second or third terrifying giant creature
may appear in another place.

00:21:06.458 --> 00:21:10.000
However, we will continue moving forward.

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:12.750
In order to solve all
the mysteries in the world,

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:16.875
the Hajime Mutsuki troop's journey
will continue without end.

00:21:16.875 --> 00:21:19.000
With those new feelings in our hearts,

00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:22.917
we, the film crew, left this land behind us.

00:21:26.667 --> 00:21:28.125
"Preview"

00:21:30.250 --> 00:21:31.375
That's...

00:21:31.375 --> 00:21:32.042
No way!

00:21:32.042 --> 00:21:33.750
Oh no, this is bad!

00:21:33.750 --> 00:21:36.667
"Is there really a giant alien on
the mysterious UFO base on the moon?"

00:21:36.667 --> 00:21:39.667
"Look forward to it"

00:21:39.667 --> 00:21:42.042
"Look forward to it"
"Broadcast date pending"

00:21:43.917 --> 00:21:49.333
<i>Accelerating to chase that cloud</i>

00:21:49.333 --> 00:21:54.542
<i>I stretch my hand out over and over,</i>
<i>but it won't reach</i>

00:21:54.542 --> 00:21:59.958
<i>That hidden lie and stagnant past</i>

00:21:59.958 --> 00:22:08.417
<i>I wonder if they will both melt away</i>
<i>in the warmth flowing by</i>

00:22:17.208 --> 00:22:22.458
<i>The sound of the rain</i>

00:22:22.458 --> 00:22:27.792
<i>Bouncing off as it falls</i>

00:22:27.792 --> 00:22:33.125
<i>I'm reflected in a puddle</i>

00:22:33.125 --> 00:22:36.833
<i>That makes my image shake</i>

00:22:36.833 --> 00:22:42.542
<i>Even so, it's the same urge again</i>

00:22:42.542 --> 00:22:48.000
<i>Accelerating to chase that cloud</i>

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:53.167
<i>I stretch my hand out over and over,</i>
<i>but it won't reach</i>

00:22:53.167 --> 00:22:58.625
<i>That hidden lie and stagnant past</i>

00:22:58.625 --> 00:23:06.250
<i>I wonder if they will both melt away</i>
<i>in the warmth flowing by</i>

